Yes.

If all bloops are razzies, and all razzies are lazzies, then every bloop must also be a lazzie. This follows from the transitive property: anything in the set of bloops is in the set of razzies, and everything in the set of razzies is in the set of lazzies, so all bloops are contained within the set of lazzies.
